#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166650 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/id #uuid "03bebdcd-5908-5c60-b35a-1c8f59593afd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9577" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/0f4f0de23892a6f76642f8c7e5d3a6112a8ffa2d9f50000cd974f293a7d8b3b6.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-1)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^2 + (y - (-1))^2 = 2^2 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nx^2 + (y+1)^2 = 4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166651 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "04c9673b-e4e5-508d-acc7-ea0888f2cf87" :question/math-academy-id "e-9578" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/d3895bafe045f7e460887aee41bf390fdda753fed87eaab14f4a29ddb792267c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{4^2} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{y^2}{16} = 1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166652 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/id #uuid "58850b39-db80-532d-9f60-808a215da76c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9579" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/a92eae1ab0af29ea895b570c95199ece1e292c09953ebb2dabbb7c6e2d422d6c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(3,-2).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\ny^2 = 4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x = 3$ and $y = -2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 4 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\ny^2 = \\dfrac{4}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2}{3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0a1ad6f-963a-565a-aa1a-b61af06808ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344404} {:answer/id #uuid "d09220f9-cee3-5516-b509-77130086e7dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344405} {:answer/id #uuid "9693e067-ab7c-5cc3-84e5-46b3cea80a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344406} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1f2a12-5cfd-558b-b0c5-5769e6744966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344407} {:answer/id #uuid "eb6eb67f-7548-5252-99cc-de0dcaaee9b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0a1ad6f-963a-565a-aa1a-b61af06808ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344404} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c74aa46-d3ec-5c33-a2e7-3102445c4b51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7bda6d9-2c04-5573-bcfc-a6e69eb3e22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127493" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/f24d078ca0dc57ebd12778b7862683b0289e9c0d4c664639bd210dcc1f7c6d1b.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={4}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(16) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47097999-98b6-5670-8195-340436682d72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344411} {:answer/id #uuid "e98a27c2-fe1a-5c99-8192-a42813ca62c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(x+1)y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344412} {:answer/id #uuid "f68d9db6-a081-523e-abc1-8a38c58b966a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344413} {:answer/id #uuid "d01b4e02-8bc2-50f5-8a2f-d8ba9f925df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344414} {:answer/id #uuid "47205664-36e4-5beb-85c8-6dc57fbad80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d01b4e02-8bc2-50f5-8a2f-d8ba9f925df3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344414} :answer-field/id #uuid "eeea34fc-8fe7-598f-b1a6-465bcec53034" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d6ad7e4-7acd-5527-83e9-b8c007bd5d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-127497" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/a3ca092dc7c0668ac465d4832b91a2b831af057ff22e357b4e7105bfb454ea18.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x-1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffbfdf84-89ac-501d-9d0e-a8247119c053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x+1)}{y-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344418} {:answer/id #uuid "c950d74c-c1ed-5acd-b68d-2fc1b6c46651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-x}{y+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344419} {:answer/id #uuid "90dd0c2b-eda3-55eb-83ec-8fdf22adb1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344420} {:answer/id #uuid "6b029d17-737c-570e-bcdd-c02a1295a428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x+1)(y+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344421} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce1ddc8-bd80-565b-afac-6b778dff1842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)(1-y)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90dd0c2b-eda3-55eb-83ec-8fdf22adb1cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{1-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344420} :answer-field/id #uuid "86d9054f-01f4-5cdb-a841-f3ee6daaf735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8addafb3-53aa-51de-9e83-4de2a2f51ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127499" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/2f08e0a0d1fd855f2d179ac65dbdf5d022f3488b85c78b5cbb507f12bd69487e.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(-1,1)$ and has a radius of $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^{2}+(y-1)^{2}={1}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+1)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)+2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{y-1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+1}{1-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c655c1c-963b-55a7-b7bf-dec798042a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(y+2)}{x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344425} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8ea6f6-2e4d-571e-bf91-2d7769a063d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{x-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344426} {:answer/id #uuid "b34aea3d-09f0-5e22-b539-71b51116cd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x-3)}{y-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344427} {:answer/id #uuid "3b41ad3c-2218-5978-9b6c-81d5188c6da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344428} {:answer/id #uuid "f76c4155-0a9e-5f83-a0b6-63f2b205a1e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b41ad3c-2218-5978-9b6c-81d5188c6da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344428} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c789b73-49a2-5de2-96d3-a48b39bfd1e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e4ebd8d-39de-546f-8e4d-90d9fb45b65a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127500" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/78ad1a6835bb71441f77a3ca2bbdc93a42635e0386cda35fbe5fc9b0c9f48677.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(-3,-2)$ and has a radius of $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(-3))^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={2}^{2}\\,⟹\\,(x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+3)^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+3)+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+3}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1331279e-1a5f-5f6f-9104-0c88e1f9f6d0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0ef93cb-7366-593e-ad38-c818c0850449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y+2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344432} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe66a0a-b5f6-53f9-9d7d-f33f4f488aa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344433} {:answer/id #uuid "d5031e23-dc2a-5f7b-8b9b-c55cb0125296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344434} {:answer/id #uuid "c32e4cd8-b012-591c-ba56-2197b57f0567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344435} {:answer/id #uuid "468a1494-fc5b-56b4-8316-13c1b67b633a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+2}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c32e4cd8-b012-591c-ba56-2197b57f0567" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{y+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344435} :answer-field/id #uuid "e144559b-9b8c-55c6-b20f-b375f68afb7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40004000-9c6b-5eec-bba4-63cd6ff30027" :question/math-academy-id "q-127502" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/812f88e913650b7924fc13acc7adde999819d0011fa547a7e0ad73cb37e3939f.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the circle shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our circle is centered at $(0,-2)$ and has a radius of $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-0)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2}={3}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+2)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+2)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2d1eeee-b88b-5404-a208-8c755d6bbb83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344439} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff31bf6-d036-5225-9c74-7c7d2f5d7583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344440} {:answer/id #uuid "58dff48e-4a47-5d9a-afd3-6347781c5e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344441} {:answer/id #uuid "145f6ecf-44af-569a-a98c-4122f8bd30eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344442} {:answer/id #uuid "db115e32-ef0d-5005-a32d-6c76a6d74aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "145f6ecf-44af-569a-a98c-4122f8bd30eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344442} :answer-field/id #uuid "86480513-0d44-532c-a1de-77938bf94631" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54ca6e99-2d40-50f1-ab5d-d366e33a931c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127511" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/c0295c7cdc1abc16273efda842a0aa7a892ece2f5dda5e29f7baab25320b23ec.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bf2eb4d-a9a6-51be-9e7b-251ac2e1e6ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344446} {:answer/id #uuid "b729a707-05d6-58d1-85ec-da9d68ed80ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344447} {:answer/id #uuid "7c56a228-50dc-5d98-8843-7ac127ebb564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{25x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344448} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9ceb74-c983-513b-89cb-3a0e146f4ba8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5y}{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344449} {:answer/id #uuid "39b6ba78-6d82-5e48-b0b6-e28dbe5fa4ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{5y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bf2eb4d-a9a6-51be-9e7b-251ac2e1e6ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344446} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c37885e-4d3c-5bf9-949b-bcbf010fc8e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5af86b8f-c0e9-5ee9-8670-c65d273b6ede" :question/math-academy-id "q-127512" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/43e8ed1ee117ccd10f0e3aa03fc8db8ec1db6c076689e9072e1e22e048dfc279.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $5$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{25}+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{25y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7e60346-4568-55b7-a5cc-f94ec75f2635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344453} {:answer/id #uuid "f47d2eb6-75c2-590c-9cb3-8deda81c6565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344454} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc9ad94-483f-5b98-b11b-095698178da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344455} {:answer/id #uuid "07d854e1-c60f-5174-989e-53094c48656e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344456} {:answer/id #uuid "1e3f94bb-82fa-5461-a7bc-aca0d5c3d007" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07d854e1-c60f-5174-989e-53094c48656e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344456} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee84cdf-55a4-5fde-9bdb-bb1dfed88b9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58f5d542-39f0-5cac-afa1-00eeca4dd963" :question/math-academy-id "q-127513" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/f8effaf21270245ed6f8df63d2e430483756f47537b1c7325e88acc5286544db.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{25x}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9790fbca-a081-5427-978a-36f24620a867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344460} {:answer/id #uuid "c558ba65-aeb1-57de-8c3d-b32bf211126f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344461} {:answer/id #uuid "04f15475-5162-5e64-a228-2c3254368ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344462} {:answer/id #uuid "fee356ad-1580-5ba0-8d25-e9aab8bc18d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344463} {:answer/id #uuid "611cea9b-7480-5f59-9b8d-69f8551048e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04f15475-5162-5e64-a228-2c3254368ed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344462} :answer-field/id #uuid "c86e583c-232f-56ce-868c-d6efb5f81db7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce6382e-085b-5d98-89eb-3fb7ac90eace" :question/math-academy-id "q-127514" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/547b79b566d2914db4a63997cd5fc9f02dd1517b8dcd5e53cde8c07ac5ca05a2.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $3$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{9}+2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a33399f-b4d5-5f6b-91dc-15f5d9c56441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344467} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddc44c9-4abe-55d8-a64e-28ed5e5f40a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344468} {:answer/id #uuid "e67d125f-f728-5d89-af9e-0c6b8bf97a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344469} {:answer/id #uuid "06e327f2-4296-5c9c-9184-d6aa1f3cd505" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344470} {:answer/id #uuid "60e8abb3-d012-53bc-b238-57ef1a7b0fb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60e8abb3-d012-53bc-b238-57ef1a7b0fb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344471} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b8c0afa-2f73-51dd-b12f-075a7560de71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04522178-100e-570d-8bab-ad0415e9727a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127515" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/5eedb15e515993bdc8a2ee37ab4c7c0e0225b9d2118d5d60e8593de5ea56f199.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above." :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-1,2).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1$ and $y=2$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 4 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-4x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665f1313-3d2e-5cee-87ee-d5ba94bc57ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x-3)}{3y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344474} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3772bf-6806-527b-a9af-4abca19338f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344475} {:answer/id #uuid "798265db-ae30-5a90-88cb-5a0dc1981d75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y-3)}{9x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344476} {:answer/id #uuid "1a348b22-7ab4-5172-970d-494351019936" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{2(x-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344477} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b16115-bff3-5f6f-a0c5-7bbb4bc73e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{4(y-3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae3772bf-6806-527b-a9af-4abca19338f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344475} :answer-field/id #uuid "b983e182-647e-5d29-b7d3-d8698920c28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1560c805-819c-53d3-a13d-4bf1ec1c493c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127526" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/e4c39b409f6049a4fdead506c329d232820876c37ede9540adfeade2d7c1b9dc.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(3,0)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-3)}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-3)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68d7507c-f55c-5954-ac65-0cf703224c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68d7507c-f55c-5954-ac65-0cf703224c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{10y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344481} :answer-field/id #uuid "749c93a5-d3b1-5006-bf44-90d33b709217" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2b3af54-e038-57d8-a207-5e5ccf9719d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-312780" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/b269001ff5a3a1a1d86125157ee2f5b77d89ebcf0041f8d403dbc931b796c5e8.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(5,7).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ and $y=7$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 49 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{49}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{5}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{49}{5}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{5} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{49}{10y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7d34b16-60c1-51af-9fe1-468101c90595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344484} {:answer/id #uuid "760f2f3d-830d-5146-aa04-9bd806fc2dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760f2f3d-830d-5146-aa04-9bd806fc2dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344485} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d3e96e6-c7ae-587c-ac24-448fb703e9e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dc1c970f-aca1-5725-85b7-89d4b93cb963" :question/math-academy-id "q-342215" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/c403f11093b76facafbecb72bcc413640ac67fe6ed73d6b64374230f39e29aba.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-3,-1).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ and $y=-1$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{2} & =4p(-3) \\\\ 1 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{3}x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{6y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74f93b34-cd84-502a-8305-9077d001f0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74f93b34-cd84-502a-8305-9077d001f0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2dccab9-ea02-5dfe-8085-82f012907ae9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8dbbe6ed-99af-53ff-93a0-b57eb15687b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-342218" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/7367cb4ae1feb4e18b98b712687ceb4a1db67f8c9e4965af3ffd1253a827f346.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the left-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe general equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=-6x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-6x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{3}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53a1649d-4279-5b7c-839c-728f333b2c3f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to a Parabola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c34001-0779-582f-a2a0-b18d4e8681a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344491} {:answer/id #uuid "009d0a8e-0c8c-57f7-be89-961c854405ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344492}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c34001-0779-582f-a2a0-b18d4e8681a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344491} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2daf528-e450-5fbf-9dfc-7993564ab098" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248059b8-c797-518d-848e-0b4117c22754" :question/math-academy-id "q-342354" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/85d75e0f3a9f2a30282d1f1754b0c46da49e8f73ff2a858c856ba5492eb21cca.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the right-opening parabola shown above. Express the answer in terms of the variable $y.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The diagram shows that the parabola has its vertex at $O,$ and passes through the point $(8,-8).$\n\nThe standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola whose vertex is at $(0,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=8$ and $y=-8$ into the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-8)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of our parabola is \n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=8x.\n$$\n\nFinally, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x) \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{4}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
